Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["There are 5 examples of timing and results:\n(1) Example 1- \
Example 3 provide timing results for the spherical cases shown in Table I ",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 1.]],
 StyleBox["in the manuscript",
  FontFamily->"Times New Roman",
  FontSize->28,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 1.]],
 StyleBox[".\n(2)Example 4 contains 3 deformed cases shown in Table I ",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 1.]],
 StyleBox["in the manuscript",
  FontFamily->"Times New Roman",
  FontSize->28,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 1.]],
 StyleBox[".\n(3) The simple Lanczos code is validated in the p=22, k=6 \
case.The  Lanczos code for diagonalizing Hp is used for p=22, k=11 and p=29, \
k=8 cases presented in Example 4. \n(4) Example 5 provides the ",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 1.]],
 StyleBox["multi-coupling coefficients shown in Table II in the manuscript.",
  FontFamily->"Times New Roman",
  FontSize->28,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 1.]],
 StyleBox["  \n(5) The code for deterministic phase fixing for each \
eigenvector is presented in examples 1-3 and 5.",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 1.]]
}], "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.875969869810183*^9, 3.87596990407795*^9}, {
